(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[5 1 "// Attribute lookup (PY5c; CPython's _PyType_Lookup, PyObject_GenericGetAttr and SetAttr,"] [6 1 "// type_getattro and type_setattro): data descriptors before the instance's __dict__, non-data"] [7 1 "// descriptors after; the built-in types' attributes (tp_getset, tp_members) as GetSets beside their"] [8 1 "// dictionaries, and their slots seen as methods (slot wrappers) as CPython's add_operators puts them"] [9 1 "// in the type's dictionary."] [11 1 "// GetSet is a built-in type's attribute (getset_descriptor): Get, and Set (nil: read-only; v nil:"] [12 1 "// delete)."] [18 2 "// member: a PyMemberDef's attribute, member_descriptor where CPython has one (types.MemberDescriptorType is"] [19 2 "// type(FunctionType.__globals__)); read-only ones say \"readonly attribute\""] [21 2 "// shared: 3.15's one __dict__ or __weakref__ descriptor of every class (object's; queue 237), its repr without"] [22 2 "// an owner"] [37 1 "// getsetOrder: each type's getsets' names in their declaration order (its __dict__'s order, queue 313)"] [40 1 "// AddGetSet declares a built-in type's attribute."] [54 1 "// AddMember declares a built-in type's PyMemberDef attribute."] [60 1 "// AddMethod puts a built-in method in a built-in type's dictionary (bound to the instance by"] [61 1 "// attribute lookup: fn gets the instance first)."] [66 1 "// AddToDict puts v in a built-in type's dictionary once the runtime is ready (a dictionary's keys"] [67 1 "// are hashed by str's slot, which an init function may run before)."] [86 1 "// readyDataModel completes the built-in types' dictionaries, once."] [102 1 "// lookupAttr is _PyType_Lookup over t's MRO: each type's dictionary, its GetSets, and for a built-in"] [103 1 "// type its slots as slot wrappers; the value and the type it was found on."] [126 1 "// The type attribute cache (PY6-core, queue 200, after PY8's measurement: lookupAttr was 31-35% of a run;"] [127 1 "// CPython's method cache over tp_version_tag): each type keeps its lookups' answers by name, the absent ones"] [128 1 "// too, and drops them all when typeEpoch moves. typeEpoch moves on any change to a type's namespace (the dicts"] [129 1 "// marked ofType: an insertion, a replaced value, a deletion, a clear, popitem), on a getset added, and on an"] [130 1 "// MRO set (c3MRO's and readyTypes'), so an answer is never older than the namespaces it was read from."] [138 1 "// lookupAttrMRO is _PyType_Lookup's walk: t's MRO's dicts, then the getsets and slot wrappers of each."] [159 1 "// superLookup is lookupAttr over the part of start's MRO after typ (super's lookup)."] [188 1 "// descrGet is a found attribute's __get__ (obj nil: from the class); a built-in method found on a"] [189 1 "// built-in type is bound to obj (its value for a built-in subclass's instance)."] [195 3 "// object's methods take the instance itself (PY6d's REQUEST: __reduce_ex__'s class); objectDescr is"] [196 3 "// methodDescrs[b] == ObjectType without the map's lookup on every method's binding (queue 210)"] [208 1 "// methodDescrs are the built-in types' methods that left their type's dict through the class (T.name: CPython's"] [209 1 "// method_descriptor), each with its type: put in a class's dict (socket.socket.getsockname = saved, test_socket's"] [210 1 "// test_injected_authentication_failure) such a method still binds to the instance, as a method descriptor does,"] [211 1 "// where a built-in function there (class A: f = len) does not."] [216 1 "// instanceDict is o's __dict__, nil when it has none."] [255 1 "// InstanceDictHook is the __dict__ of an object of another package (arbace/pyctypes' C-born objects whose type has a"] [256 1 "// tp_dictoffset: the dict their memory holds; queue 268), nil when it has none."] [259 1 "// The attribute instructions' inline caches (202b; PEP 659's LOAD_ATTR and STORE_ATTR caches, after the type"] [260 1 "// version tag): load-attr and store-attr of an object whose type takes the generic path keep, per instruction, the"] [261 1 "// type they last saw and lookupAttr's answer for it, valid while typeEpoch has not moved (the epoch the type"] [262 1 "// attribute cache's own answers hold by, attr.go's lookupAttr), so a hit compares two words where lookupAttr hashes"] [263 1 "// the name into the type's cache."] [269 2 "// di: where the instance's dict held the name when it was last found there (queue 210; CPython's"] [270 2 "// LOAD_ATTR_INSTANCE_VALUE's index): an entry holding the name's very str (co_names are interned) is the name's"] [274 1 "// lookupAttrAt is lookupAttr(tp, name) through the cache of c's instruction pc."] [280 1 "// attrSite is an instruction's caches: the last types it saw, the latest first (queue 210: richards' four task"] [281 1 "// classes share their methods' instructions, and one entry missed at every change of type)."] [286 1 "// attrSites are every code's inline caches (queue 241), swept by gc.collect: an entry whose epoch is past holds a type"] [287 1 "// and the value found, which CPython's caches (a version tag) do not keep alive (WeakMethod's test_method_dead: the"] [288 1 "// method deleted from its class stays in the site that loaded it). attrSwept is the epoch of the last sweep."] [294 1 "// sweepAttrSites clears the stale entries of every inline cache, once per type epoch."] [311 1 "// attrICAt is c's instruction pc's cache entry holding lookupAttr(tp, name)."] [334 34 "// tp's old entry, else the oldest, dropped"] [339 1 "// dictEntryAt is the position of the entry of d holding name itself, through the hint *di (kept up to date); -1"] [340 1 "// when d does not hold name (an equal str in its place is found, but not kept as the hint)."] [352 1 "// loadAttrAt is load-attr at c's instruction pc: GetAttr, its generic path's lookup through the instruction's cache."] [361 3 "// genericGetAttrFound's instance dict through the hint (queue 210)"] [383 1 "// storeAttrAt is store-attr (v nil: delete-attr) at c's instruction pc: SetAttr, its generic path's lookup through"] [384 1 "// the instruction's cache."] [393 3 "// genericSetAttrFound's dict.Set through the hint: a value replaced in place (queue 210)"] [396 5 "// store_instance_attr's MODIFIED, the value the same or not (queue 274)"] [406 21 "// the usual case: the name inserted last"] [413 1 "// GenericGetAttr is object.__getattribute__."] [420 1 "// genericGetAttrFound is GenericGetAttr with lookupAttr's answer for o's type tp."] [438 1 "// GenericSetAttr is object.__setattr__ (v nil: object.__delattr__)."] [445 1 "// genericSetAttrFound is GenericSetAttr with lookupAttr's answer for o's type tp."] [473 1 "// typeGetAttr is type.__getattribute__: the metatype's data descriptors, then the type's MRO, then"] [474 1 "// the metatype's other attributes."] [484 3 "// _PyType_Lookup of t's MRO assigns the version tag a watched modification clears (queue 274); the"] [485 3 "// metatype's data descriptors (__name__, __dict__) answer before it"] [492 29 "// a method descriptor leaving its type"] [500 4 "// a built-in type's class and static methods know their type for __qualname__"] [523 1 "// typeSetAttr is type.__setattr__: a class's attribute, its slots updated for a special one."] [534 3 "// tp_name: a static type's module and name ('compression.zstd.ZstdCompressor'; builtins' bare), a frozen class's"] [535 3 "// name (queue 270b: PyType_Freeze)"] [554 26 "// a C type's slots are its own (queue 270b: its dict changes alone)"] [557 19 "// type_setattro's PyType_Modified: the type watchers (queue 274)"] [562 1 "// SetAttr is setattr(o, name, v); v nil is delattr."] [570 1 "// DelAttr is delattr(o, name)."] [573 1 "// GetAttrOptional is getattr(o, name) with nil, not an AttributeError, when there is no such attribute."] [576 1 "// LookupSpecial is a special method's lookup on o's type (_PyObject_LookupSpecial): bound to o, or nil."] [585 1 "// getAttrOptional is getattr(o, name, None) without the None: nil when there is no such attribute."] [597 1 "// callBound calls a method found on self's type bound to self (CPython's vectorcall of an unbound"] [598 1 "// method with self first, or __get__ then the call); owner is the type of self's MRO it was found on"] [599 1 "// (lookupAttr's), nil when not known."] [606 4 "// wrapperdescr_call's check (bpo-37619: a wrapper of the wrong class in a class's dict)"] [612 4 "// a built-in function in a class's dict is no method descriptor: called without the instance, as"] [613 4 "// descrGet's rule and lookup_maybe_method (class C: __call__ = len; typing.NewType's __call__ = _idfunc,"] [614 4 "// queue 207)"] [618 4 "// object's own methods take the instance itself (descrGet's rule, PY6d's R2), as for"] [619 4 "// object.__reduce_ex__ of a class deriving from a built-in type (PY6g's F2: random.Random's pickling)"] [675 2 "// a descriptor's own attributes (PY6a: inspect's getattr_static reads __name__ and __objclass__)"] [691 2 "// object's attributes"] [693 2 "// a built-in type with a dictionary shows it itself (BaseException's, function's, module's); a class's is"] [694 2 "// subtype_getsets_full's, in the dict of the class that adds it (addLayoutDescrs): object has none"] [702 2 "// BaseException's attributes (exceptions.c's BaseException_getset and members)"] [761 1 "// unpackAll is the items of an iterable."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[73 32] [77 32] [116 31] [143 31] [147 28] [151 35] [163 6] [163 20] [169 9] [169 23] [172 31] [176 28] [180 35] [191 26] [202 33] [303 28] [320 23] [342 18] [360 27] [368 41] [392 27] [394 21] [402 32] [405 34] [426 28] [449 34] [488 33] [489 27] [503 34] [507 34] [512 34] [529 35] [550 38] [564 32] [626 33] [647 18] [744 58]]} (go/file "attr.go" :imports [

